        "system": {
          "actionType": {
            "value": "passive"
          },
          "actions": {
            "value": null
          },
          "category": "class",
          "description": {
            "value": "<p>Stories serve as beacons in the night, illuminating valuable knowledge even if the tale itself misses the mark. When you @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Offer Story]{Offer a Story} about any topic, you can choose that illumination in place of the normal benefits of Offer Story. You receive a +1 status bonus on checks to @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.actionspf2e.Item.Recall Knowledge] for the duration and can Recall Knowledge about the topic of the story as a free action. The creature you share a story with can choose this benefit even if you did not.</p>\n<p>The bonus increases to +2 if you are a master of Religion and +3 if you are legendary.</p>"
          },
          "level": {
            "value": 6
          },
